  "qualification_limits": [
    "Embedded disposable producer, import destination and proposal Scope only; no user store opened. No server/HTTP or two-engine release sweep.",
    "Command 20 initially refused the unprefixed fixed Issue ID after import. That refusal is retained in the local raw evidence. The article adds --force for the two practice Issue IDs; the corrected continuation completed commands 20\u201370 without rerunning or relabeling the initial 19 observations.",
    "One alternative creation block was executed independently to avoid recreating an existing identity.",
    "An earlier discovery probe assumed an unguarded update would refuse; it succeeded, making that probe\u2019s following guard stale. The original probe is retained and is not called a passing journey.",
    "Illustrative compact proposal displays are authored, not copied terminal output. Full stored data was checked separately.",
    "make check-docs could not start its Bazel gate because bazel is unavailable. Plain-Go docsync and direct freshness checks passed; they are not relabeled as Bazel qualification."
  ],
  "release_question": "Does the final Preview 3 cut include bd memory remember/recall/memories/forget and typed remember creation from the newer CLI design? The selected binary does not expose nested content verbs (memory recall returns group help); the draft uses working top-level content commands and generic typed creation."
}
